On Friday 14 March 2003 4:40 pm, Pavel Machek wrote:
>
> So... S4 does actually work for you?
> 									Pavel

Yes it does work. I finally figured out that it was using the "swap" partition 
to hibernate and not the "a0" parition.

Don't forget: Have to give the "resume=/dev/<your_swap_partition_here>" to the 
kernel at boot.

If you do a normal boot, your swap partition is scrambled and you'll have to 
reformat it.

Shawn



